From: ikwfahmi <mikhwanfahmi4@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:25:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] gui: Own threaded actions independently of theme pages

The render thread can reload a theme after the worker requests reload,
deleting the page-owned GUIAction while ActionThread still iterates its
actions. Give each worker batch a standalone executor and copy the action
strings before starting it. Release that executor when the batch ends.

Signed-off-by: ikwfahmi <mikhwanfahmi4@gmail.com>
Change-Id: I938fe07b4dc4bac0be41d45e55a66d5f63010c16

--- a/gui/action.cpp
+++ b/gui/action.cpp
@@ -93,8 +93,15 @@
   {
     ActionThread *this_;
     GUIAction *act;
-    ThreadData(ActionThread * this_, GUIAction * act):this_(this_), act(act)
-    {
+    ThreadData(ActionThread * this_, GUIAction * source):this_(this_), act(new GUIAction(nullptr))
+    {
+      // A theme reload may destroy the page that owns the source action.
+      // Keep the worker's executor and action strings independent of it.
+      act->mActions = source->mActions;
+    }
+    ~ThreadData()
+    {
+      delete act;
     }
   };
 
